    "title": "Charleston grocery stores open on Easter Sunday 2026",
    "text": "(Getty Images) Posted: Apr 3, 2026 / 10:34 AM EDT Updated: Apr 3, 2026 / 10:34 AM EDT (Getty Images) by: Claudia Landis Posted: Apr 3, 2026 / 10:34 AM EDT Updated: Apr 3, 2026 / 10:34 AM EDT CHARLESTON, S.C. (WCBD) – Whether you’re hosting a lovely Easter lunch or visiting friends and family, you might find yourself hopping over to the grocery store for those last-minute goodies. And if you are not celebrating Easter, it is a good idea to know which stores are open before you head out for your shopping trip. Here is an update on the statuses of grocery and convenience stores for April 5: ALDI – CLOSED Bert’s Market – Open 24/7, 365 days a year Costco – CLOSED CVS Pharmacy – Open, hours vary by location Earth Fare – Open, 9 a.m. to 7 p.m. Food Lion – Open during normal business hours Harris Teeter – Open during normal business hours Lidl – Open during normal business hours Piggly Wiggly – Most open, hours vary by location Publix – CLOSED Rite Aid – Open during normal business hours Sam’s Club – CLOSED Target – CLOSED Trader Joe’s – Open during normal business hours Walgreens – Most open, hours vary by location Walmart – Open during regular business hours Whole Foods – Open, hours vary by location. Hours may vary by location; check your nearest store ahead of time. TOP CLICKS AT COUNTON2.COM BestReviews.com - Top picks to make everyone happy",
